# Completed transaction

Say a task is complete only when you have confirmation. A command being accepted is not the same as a device reaching the requested state. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Use it after a setup flow, to show what was saved and the most useful next action. Keep any feedback request optional and separate from the confirmed result.

## Structure and behaviour

Name the completed task, and include a reference only if the underlying system supplies one. If the device has not responded, say so and explain what remains ([WG-044](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-044)). Keep a route back to the relevant native page. A short action usually needs a local status message, not a whole completion page. [Action requests and results](../../home-assistant/action-results.html) owns the request, pending, confirmed and failed wording.

## Home Assistant boundary

No government /done route, satisfaction service or promotional content is added. Do not show "Completed" because the person pressed a button or an animation ended. Keep saved, enabled and running apart ([WG-035](../../content/writing-guidelines/states-and-errors.html#wg-035)).

